SUMMARY:Mammals of the Central Piedmont (Monroe)
DESCRIPTION:Join Dr. Steve Fields\, curator of natural history at the Culture & Heritage Museums of York County\, for a fascinating look at more than 20 years of research documenting nearly 50 mammal species across the historically overlooked and understudied Carolina Piedmont. From familiar species to new arrivals like the armadillo\, this ongoing research offers a glimpse into the region’s changing wildlife and environment. \nREGISTER HERE
URL:https://ncwf.org/event/mammals-of-the-central-piedmont-monroe/
CATEGORIES:Featured
